ore lore the  Fallen Hawks were not just some random  band of explorers investigating the  Eternal City they were a random band of  explorers ordered to investigate the  Eternal City we can learn even more  about this Expedition from a shield some  of the Hawks carry called the inverted  Hawk heater Shield it reads a  medium-sized metal shield easier to  handle than a kite Shield the inverted  Hawk is the emblem of the company of  slaves ordered to explore the Eternal  City this gives us a fuller picture of  the Hawks not as Noble explorers but  slaves forced to Embark underground  without enough supplies for their  Journey the fact that the hawk emblem on  their Shield is inverted May indicate  either their Journey below the surface  or their status as slaves it appears on  their inverted Hawk Tower Shield as well  but this Shield's description doesn't  offer up any more lore if the Hawks are  slaves then it Bears asking who is their  master who sent them underground to  explore the Eternal City there are a few  candidates for explanation but nothing  we can say for certain first there's the  crust they bear the inverted Hawk along  with their corresponding title as Fallen  Hawks the hawk is a symbol of stormvale  as we read from the hawk Crest wooden  Shield a tall medium-sized wooden Shield  light for its size and easy to handle  adorned with a long forgotten crest of  Stormville ancient in Design This Shield  does note that it is easy to handle  somewhat like the inverted Hawk heater  Shield there are plenty of Hawk  Connections in Stormville from the storm  Hawk King to the grafted Hawks to the  true storm bringing back a host of hawks  when nepheli takes the throne if this is  the connection then the Fallen Hawks may  have once been soldiers of Stormville  maybe they serve the stormlord that  Godfrey faced if so we would have an  explanation as to their slavery soldiers  of the old Lord they could have been  bound and chained with their Lord's  defeat we know 