he location of macron  by Going Underground through the well in  the Mist wood of lim grave  you can see no cron up above only we  failed to find a path leading to the  City blinds made a good go of it but I'm  afraid this has him quite stumped to be  honest  I'm not sure where to go from here  the line about years of expeditions  makes it sound like the exploration of  the Hawks but the fact that they haven't  found a path seems odd yes the Hawks  didn't make it back to the surface to  tell of their path but if the Hawks were  in Ronnie's charge it's weird to not  have followed up on their disappearance  it would make sense for Ronnie or  possibly her ancestors to have sent a  search party to nokron to find the blade  and we can see that the Fallen Hawks are  still searching for something in the  city maybe they found the city but their  exploration did not reach its end they  might have lost their minds but they  still hold on to the one idea that drove  them there the search for the Finger  Slayer blade and they keep digging  mindlessly propelled by that one drive  to me this explanation is weaker we  don't get any info on any of the hawk  connections and it's never stated that  the carrions had slaves they even saw  their trolls as equals with the troll  knight sword telling of how they are  treated as true Knights of karya and  fight arm in arm with their human  comrades as such the Fallen Hawks being  ordered as slaves down Into the Depths  seems out of place this brutal treatment  is more in line with the golden order  and I think we could even extend the  Finger Slayer blade searching to the  order too maybe they knew something of  nokon's treasure and its ability to harm  the greater will and its vassals this  could have motivated them to send the  Fallen Hawks to search for it and this  would again explain the Hawks and their  obsessive digging though there are a lot  of moving Parts either way from the  carrions to the stormlord so if there is  anything I missed or a conclusion that  seems unjustified due to other evidence  feel free to mention it in the comments  the Fallen Hawks are one of the most  visually striking humanoids in the game  not for any imposing or Supernatural  element but for their classic horror  look their wilted swollen State like  zombies in a permanent stasis of  starvation their bodies eternally  wasting away the head bolts missing eyes  and Crimson appendages don't help the  picture either to me they stand as one  of the game's creepiest enemies and the  lore of their enslaved investigation  matches that unnerving design they would  be right at home as a lesser creature in  one of H.P lovecraft's short stories and  they do a great job of delivering that  kind of spookiness to the underground of  the lands between if this lore  investigation of the Hawks investigation  is your kind of thing consider  subscribing to the channel or becoming a  patron on patreon both really helped me  make these videos by justifying my time  and effort with higher digital numbers  effectively unlocking my dopamine  receptors I'll be making more videos  focusing on spookiness for the rest of  October so I'll hope to see you there  with that thanks for watching and bye
 

